\subsection { \label bonus_scripts Bonus Scripts } {

   Three small helper scripts come with the Lazy Workflow:

   \table[unnumbered, marginLeft: 20px] {
      {
         { \image[height: 32px] images/Icon_KillPreviews.png }
         { \s {KillPreviews}: deletes all previews in the active image.
           Part 1's apply windows and Part 2's background finder now remove
           their previews themselves, so you only need it for leftovers, for
           example after closing Part 1's apply window without applying. }
      }
      {
         { \image[height: 32px] images/Icon_NamePreviews.png }
         { \s {NamePreviews}: if you decide to use exclusion zones in Part 2,
           draw previews over the areas to exclude and run NamePreviews. It
           renames \e all previews in the image to \c Exclude1, \c Exclude2,
           ..., so remove any other previews first. Part 2 also runs without
           exclusion zones. }
      }
      {
         { \image[height: 32px] images/Icon_PlusPreviews.png }
         { \s {+Previews} (\sref {SH +Previews} {manual}): creates 1--6 full-size previews and zooms each to
           fit. Prefixes: \c BM_ (MGC background models, with a gradient
           scale per preview), \c GC_ (continues the \c GC_, \c GC_1, ...
           numbering, matching GC's model names), \c Preview, or your own
           text. Use it after Part 1 to add more models, or on its own for
           any process where a full-size preview is useful. }
      }
   }
}
